answer:
The details and documents required for registering a high-risk AI system depend on your role (provider or deployer) and the applicable provision of Article 49:

### 1. Registration by providers under Article 49(1)
Providers of high-risk AI systems must provide and keep up to date the following details and documents [Annex VIII, Section A, points 1–5]:
* **Contact and representative details:** The name, address, and contact details of the provider [Annex VIII, Section A, points 1–5]; where submitted by another person on behalf of the provider, that person's name, address, and contact details [Annex VIII, Section A, points 1–5]; and the name, address, and contact details of the authorised representative, where applicable [Annex VIII, Section A, points 1–5].
* **System identification and purpose:** The AI system trade name and any additional unambiguous reference allowing identification and traceability [Annex VIII, Section A, points 1–5], along with a description of the intended purpose and of the components and functions supported through the AI system [Annex VIII, Section A, points 1–5].
* **Operational information and status:** A basic and concise description of the information used by the system (data, inputs) and its operating logic [Annex VIII, Section A, points 6–11], and the status of the AI system (on the market, or in service; no longer placed on the market/in service, recalled) [Annex VIII, Section A, points 6–11].
* **Market information:** Any Member States in which the system has been placed on the market, put into service, or made available in the Union [Annex VIII, Section A, points 6–11].
* **Required documents and certificates:** 
  * A copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 [Annex VIII, Section A, points 6–11].
  * Where applicable, the type, number, and expiry date of the certificate issued by the notified body, the name or identification number of that notified body, and a scanned copy of that certificate [Annex VIII, Section A, points 6–11].

*(Note: Personal data in the EU database includes the names and contact details of natural persons who are responsible for registering the system and legally authorized to represent the provider or deployer [Art. 71(5)].)*

---

### 2. Registration by providers under Article 49(2) (Annex III systems considered not high-risk)
If a provider considers an AI system referred to in Annex III to be not high-risk under Article 6(3), it must document its assessment before placing it on the market or putting it into service, and submit the following under Article 49(2) [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6], [Art. 6(4)]:
* Name, address, and contact details of the provider [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6];
* Name, address, and contact details of the person submitting information on the provider’s behalf, if applicable [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6];
* Name, address, and contact details of the authorised representative, where applicable [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6];
* The AI system trade name and any additional unambiguous reference allowing identification and traceability [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6];
* A description of the intended purpose of the AI system [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6];
* The condition or conditions under Article 6(3) based on which the system is considered not high-risk [Annex VIII, Section B, points 1–6].

---

### 3. Registration by deployers under Article 49(3)
Deployers registering high-risk AI systems must submit and keep up to date [Annex VIII, Section C, points 1–5]:
* The name, address, and contact details of the deployer [Annex VIII, Section C, points 1–5];
* The name, address, and contact details of the person submitting information on behalf of the deployer [Annex VIII, Section C, points 1–5];
* The URL of the entry of the AI system in the EU database by its provider [Annex VIII, Section C, points 1–5];
* A summary of the findings of the fundamental rights impact assessment conducted in accordance with Article 27 [Annex VIII, Section C, points 1–5];
* Where applicable, a summary of the data protection impact assessment carried out in accordance with Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 as specified in Article 26(8) [Annex VIII, Section C, points 1–5].

---

### 4. Registration for testing in real world conditions (Article 60)
For high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III undergoing testing in real world conditions, the registration details comprise [Annex IX]:
* A Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing [Annex IX];
* Name and contact details of the provider/prospective provider and deployers involved [Annex IX];
* A brief description of the system, its intended purpose, and other necessary identification information [Annex IX];
* A summary of the main characteristics of the testing plan [Annex IX];
* Information on the suspension or termination of the testing [Annex IX].

This explanation reflects the Act's statutory criteria for your situation; this is not legal advice.

